{"id": "EUVD-2026-86944", "enisaUuid": "3098cda7-71f7-365e-829d-006b2addc5a3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: rate limit unmapped SID errors\n\nA client can include many structurally valid but unmapped SIDs in a DACL.\nLogging every mapping failure lets one request generate hundreds of kernel\nerror messages.\n\nRate limit the message to prevent an authenticated client from flooding\nthe kernel log.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3005d43143096321cc857645a9d48ef4ffde8bcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/674aabf554bdaffcf25f145bf32c8b4f510f7916", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/486876f957456721b5e51af532235db4c6f7bd47", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13af319c1efec0b45fb5c1b16830eb0888b3fd1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30dbb08777b9a611d7d9193c040f382fbd0e7562", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54cb2a909996346ac6a8a3beac96c07b3dcba584", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/feca5e70fc963b088377b20879e8cd8237c2fd7d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vpc3-747g-g72v", "CVE-2026-98113"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "099e52c1-61f1-35f6-a1f3-82e20c17237f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <30dbb08777b9a611d7d9193c040f382fbd0e7562"}, {"id": "28ff36d2-dedb-3bd0-9ff3-791d4555afad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "2c716603-a496-3b38-ac95-fc5f4c0b036f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "33b0e755-e15e-3489-8c0c-045052faddd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "3fed4fce-0ac7-301e-ac7b-fea93e1807a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"},